$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\dfrac{x^3+3x^2+2x}{x+2}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{x(x+2)(x+1)}{(x+2)}\qquad\gray{\text{Factor numerator & denominator}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{{x}\cancel{(x+2)}(x+1)}{{}\cancel{(x+2)}}\qquad\gray{\text{Cancel out common factors}}
\\\\
&=x^2+x, \text{ for }x\neq -2
\end{align}$
